      width="300"
      height="300"
      loading="lazy"
      class="rounded-lg img-cap-300 shrink-0"
    />
    <div class="flex-1">
      <p>
        The Alfa Laval WHPX 409 Centrifuge is a self-cleaning disc-stack centrifuge designed for three-phase separation of diesel and fuel oils. With a 12.5 HP motor and a 7,125 RPM bowl, its OEM application table lists 8,400 L/h (36.98 US GPM derived) for marine diesel. <a href="/crude-oil-centrifuge/">Crude-oil</a> duty requires separate application sizing and does not inherit the diesel value.
      </p>
      <table>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><strong>Model Type</strong></td><td>Alfa Laval WHPX 409 TGD 24-60</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Rated Reference</strong></td><td>12,500 L/h (55.04 US GPM derived), source fluid unspecified; not an application capacity</td></tr>
